<code>assert object != null || \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.indexOf(object); this.get(i) == null || !this.get(i).equals(object);</code>

This assertion ensures that for every index before the first occurrence of the object in the set, the element at that index is either `null` (if the object is not `null`) or not equal to the object.--------------------<code>assert object != null || \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.indexOf(object); this.get(i) == null || !this.get(i).equals(object);</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the object is found in the set, then for every index before its first occurrence, the element at that index is either `null` (if the object is not `null`) or not equal to the object.--------------------<code>assert object != null || \forall int i; 0 <= i && i < this.indexOf(object); this.get(i) == null || !this.get(i).equals(object);</code>

This assert statement ensures that if the object is found in the set, then for every index before its first occurrence, the element at that index is either `null` (if the object is not `null`) or not equal to the object.--------------------